# ControlRig Stable Fixture Design

This note records the Phase 4 first stable ControlRig fixture.

## Fixture

- Recipe: `Docs/Research/fixtures/controlrig_piper_stable_prototype_recipe.json`
- Binding contract:
  `Docs/Research/fixtures/controlrig_piper_stable_animbp_binding_contract.json`
- Smoke: `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/Scripts/ControlRig/smoke_controlrig_stable_fixture.py`
- Target: `/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigStable/CR_Piper_StablePrototype`
- Source/preview mesh: `/Game/Cubeless/Character/Piper/SK_Piper.SK_Piper`

## Scope

The fixture is controls-only and uses the existing stable recipe transaction:

- small spine/head FK chain;
- left/right hand target and pole controls;
- left/right foot target and pole controls;
- weight/gate curves;
- one allowlisted `FRigUnit_BeginExecution` event unit;
- compile and `dependency_audit` enabled;
- save disabled by default.

The fixture does not mutate source assets, add solver units, bind an AnimBP, or
write outside `/Game/_MCP_Temp`.

The binding contract is separate from the base fixture. It targets only
`/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigStable/ABP_Piper_StablePrototype_Binding`, keeps
`save=false`, keeps `dependency_audit=true`, and keeps `expose_input_pins`
empty. After the later sample/temp input-default proof and manual review,
`input_default_gate.status=reviewed` records the scalar default
`PiperStable_GlobalStableGate_CTRL=1.0`.

## Smoke Contract

The smoke reads the JSON fixture, deletes any pre-existing temp target at the
same path, then runs:

1. `validate_recipe_json`;
2. `dry_run_recipe_json`;
3. `build_recipe_json`.

Validation and dry-run must report no target mutation. Build must report
successful compile, dependency audit, created hierarchy evidence, performed
writes, skipped save, and no cleanup suggestions.

The smoke intentionally leaves `save=false`, so no `.uasset` fixture is
promoted or serialized by default.
